  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1102 AM MST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nToday and Tomorrow...\nA ridge of high pressure will work its way into the area this \nafternoon creating fair weather, with mostly clear skies this \nafternoon and into tomorrow. Highs today will range into the mid \nto upper 60s climbing into the 70s tomorrow. Winds due switch back\nto east tonight though below 10 mph. This may help with some weak\nupslope and more low clouds Thursday morning for parts of Hudspeth\nand Otero Counties. \n\nFriday into the Weekend...\nOn Friday a upper level trough will work its way into the region,\nHighs will remain in the low to mid 70s but winds will become \nbreezy Friday afternoon through Saturday morning as an area of \nlow pressure passes north of the region. Wind gusts will be \nbetween 15-25 mph in the low lands but reach as high as 40 mph in\nhigher elevation areas. We anticipate all precipitation to remain\nnorth of our region, with dry southwesterly winds helping out \nwith that. Ridging will begin to work its way back into the area \nSaturday afternoon into Sunday creating fair weather to end the \nweekend but temperatures will be slightly cooler ranging from the \nlow to mid 60s for highs both Saturday and Sunday.\n\nEarly Next Week...\nNext week another upper level disturbance will shift into the \narea. Southwesterly winds will shift some moisture into the area, \nthis will bring a slight chance for precipitation to the area \nincluding a non zero chance for some flurries to higher elevation \nareas. Models disagree on rainfall totals so will continue to hold\noff on totals until confidence increases. With the slight chance \nof precipitation there will also be a chance for gusts between \n20-30 mph in higher elevation areas Late Monday night into \nTuesday.",
